You are building MiniDev UI, a free React + Tailwind component library.

BEFORE ANY COMPONENT:
- Read DESIGN.md. Every value comes from it. Invent nothing.
- Check if shadcn/ui already has the primitive. If yes, build on it. Never rebuild it.
- Check if Radix/Base UI has the behavior. If yes, use it. Never hand-roll focus traps,
  keyboard nav, or portal positioning.

EVERY COMPONENT MUST:
- Live under src/registry/ (ui/ for primitives, blocks/ for compositions)
- Use CVA for variants, tailwind-merge for class composition
- Be fully typed, forwardRef, spread ...props to the root
- Ship every state in DESIGN.md section "States"
- Use semantic tokens only. No literal colors, no arbitrary values, no hex
- Have zero layout shift between states
- Work in light and dark
- Include a gallery route at app/gallery/<name>/page.tsx rendering EVERY variant,
  size, and state on one page, including edge cases: long text, one character,
  no icon, icon only, empty, error, loading, RTL

AFTER EVERY BATCH:
- Run `npm run audit`. Fix every failure. Never weaken a rule to pass.
- Look at the gallery screenshot in light and dark before moving on
- Only then move to the next batch

NEVER:
- transition: all, ease, or 300ms defaults
- rgba(0,0,0,x) shadows or single-layer shadows
- a component that is skin-aware or hardcodes a color
- marking work done without viewing the screenshot
